jobs.description:
As a Logistics Employee, you will start your journey in the Value Added Services (VAS) department. Together with your team, you will make sure products are processed accurately, packed properly and prepared for shipment to customers around the world.

- Inspect incoming goods;
- Load and unload containers;
- Label and repack products when needed;
- Pick, check and prepare customer orders for shipment;
- Work closely with your colleagues to ensure everything runs smoothly.

After approximately two months, you will move to another logistics department. Here, you will learn new tasks and gain even more variety in your work. This gives you the opportunity to develop yourself into an all-round logistics employeeDo you see yourself working in a dynamic logistics environment where you can develop your skills and grow within the company? Don’t wait any longer and apply today! We will contact you as soon as possible to discuss the opportunities.

Because you will also be working with an electric pallet truck (EPT) in this position, if you do not have any prior experience with it, you will be required to complete a training course and obtain the corresponding certificate.

- You speak and understand English well;
- You are available to work full-time;
- You are willing to work in a two-shift schedule after your training period;
- You have experience working in logistics or production;
- You are motivated and enjoy working hands-on.
- Holds an EPT certificate or is willing to obtain one through Olympia.
